{
  "sn41.3:0.1": "Linked Discourses 41.3 ",
  "sn41.3:0.2": "1. With Citta ",
  "sn41.3:0.3": "With Isidatta (2nd) ",
  "sn41.3:1.1": "At one time several senior mendicants were staying near Macchikāsaṇḍa in the Wild Mango Grove. ",
  "sn41.3:1.2": "Then Citta the householder went up to them, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to them, ",
  "sn41.3:1.3": "“Sirs, would the senior monks please accept tomorrow’s meal from me?” ",
  "sn41.3:1.4": "They consented with silence. ",
  "sn41.3:1.5": "Then, knowing that the senior mendicants had consented, Citta rose from his seat, bowed, and respectfully circled them, keeping them on his right, before leaving. ",
  "sn41.3:1.6": "Then when the night had passed, the senior mendicants robed up in the morning and, taking their bowls and robes, went to Citta’s home, and sat down on the seats spread out. ",
  "sn41.3:2.1": "So he went up to them, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to the senior venerable: ",
  "sn41.3:2.2": "“Honorable Senior, there are many different views that arise in the world. For example: ",
  "sn41.3:2.3": "the cosmos is eternal, or not eternal, or finite, or infinite; the soul and the body are one and the same, or the soul is one thing, the body another; after death, a realized one still exists, or no longer exists, or both still exists and no longer exists, or neither still exists nor no longer exists. ",
  "sn41.3:2.4": "And also the sixty-two misconceptions spoken of in ‘The Divine Net’. ",
